ay depend on a host: each is ONE self-contained HTML file a person receives by any channel (Telegram, email) and opens from disk, and it makes no network request of any kind.\n\nRead first: docs/design.md (its five rules, words and colours bind both pages), verify.js, model.js (changeOneCharacter, recordOf, ordersOf), render.js, hub.js, test/order.test.mjs, and spec/SPEC.md: \"A work order, tick.work-order.v1\" and \"A receipt of version two, tick.receipt.v2\". Do not change verify.js, the spec or anything the site serves.\n\nWHAT TO BUILD\n\n1. tools/page-shell.mjs: `pageShell({ title, body, script, data })` returns a whole HTML document. It carries inline CSS following docs/design.md (paper, ink, tick, tick-wash, halt, both themes through prefers-color-scheme, one column at 400 px wide) and a system font stack, since a single file carries no font files. It carries this Content-Security-Policy meta, exactly: `default-src 'none'; script-src 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'; img-src data:; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'`. Embedded JSON goes in a `<script type=\"application/json\">` block with every `</` written `<\\/`. To inline verify.js it strips the `export ` at the start of lines, and it refuses a source that holds `</`. All the words a person reads live in one table per page, so another language later changes one table.\n\n2. tools/receipt-page.mjs: `node tools/receipt-page.mjs <receipt.json> <out.html>`, also exported as `receiptPage(receiptText)`. It refuses a file that is not a valid tick.receipt.v2, with verifyDocument's reasons. The page shows the receipt card's rows from docs/design.md, from the record: Asked by, Done by, Changed, Checked, Accepted, Landed, Cost, with a missing figure as a dash and its reason. Under them it shows the key behind each role, and when one key signed every role it says \"one company ordered, did, checked and accepted this work\". Rule 4 binds it: a \"Check it yourself\" button and a \"Change one character and check again\" button, using changeOneCharacter. Nothing is green until this browser has just verified the document: before the button it shows no verdict, and after a changed character it shows the failure with its word. When the browser cannot do Ed25519 it says so in plain words and that verify-py checks the same document.\n\n3. tools/approve-core.js: an ES module that runs in a browser and in Node, using only `crypto.subtle` and functions from verify.js (`canonicalSerialize`, `documentHash`). It exports:\n   - `makeKeys()`: an extractable Ed25519 key pair.\n   - `keyFileOf(keys)`: the text of a key file, JSON `{ schema: 'tick-buyer-key/1', pkcs8, spki }`, both base64.\n   - `keysFromFile(text)`: the keys back; it refuses anything else in plain words.\n   - `signOrder(body, { orderId, issuedAt }, keys)`: the whole tick.work-order.v1 document: schema, alg, issued_at, `coordinator: buyer:<key_id>`, order_id, order, checks_hash (the document hash of order.checks), content_hash (the document hash of order), key (SPKI in base64), key_id (the first 16 hexadecimal characters of the SHA-256 of the SPKI bytes), signature (over the UTF-8 bytes of `tick-work-order:v1:<order_id>:<content_hash>`) and limits, which are the first two lines of the spec's \"What the document says it does not establish\" for a work order, plus: `payment none means no money is held for this order: the parties pay as their job agreement says.`\n\n4. tools/approve-page.mjs: `node tools/approve-page.mjs <order-body.json> <out.html>`, also exported as `approvePage(bodyText, { orderId })`. The input is the body the spec names: what, repository, base, territory, checks, budget, deadline, acceptor, payment, from_task. It proves the body first, by signing with a throwaway key and calling verifyDocument, and refuses with its reasons. It makes the order_id once with randomUUID and embeds it, so one file approves one order. The page shows, in plain words and in this order:\n   - What you are asking for (`what`)\n   - Where (repository, and the base's first 12 characters)\n   - The files it may change\n   - What decides done (each check's `name`)\n   - The most the agents may spend (`budget.cap_usd`, or \"no limit set\")\n   - Deadline (or \"none set\")\n   - Who accepts (\"Accepted when every check passes\", or the person's name)\n   - Money: \"No money is held for this order. You pay as your job agreement says.\"\n   Then a button, \"Approve this order\". On it the page uses the loaded key or makes one, signs, and checks its own result with verifyDocument. Only then does it say \"Approved in this browser\" in green. It then offers \"Save the approved order\", which downloads `approved-order-<first 8 of the order id>.json`, and \"Copy it\", with a fallback that selects the text when the clipboard refuses. Keys: \"I have a key file\" takes a saved key through a file input, and \"Save my key\" downloads `my-tick-key.json` with these words beside it: \"Keep this file private. Anyone who has it can approve orders as you.\" A key is never sent anywhere and never appears in the saved order. When the browser cannot do Ed25519, the page says so in plain words and shows no button.\n\n5. ./README.md: a short section on the two pages: what each is for, the two commands, and that each makes no network request. docs/design.md: note that these two pages use a system font stack because a single file carries no font files, and that every other rule holds.\n\nTESTS, with node:test and no new dependency.\ntest/approve-page.test.mjs:\n   - signOrder on a sample body gives a document verifyDocument calls valid;\n   - changing one character of the signed body makes it not valid;\n   - keysFromFile(keyFileOf(keys)) gives the same key_id, and garbage is refused;\n   - approvePage refuses a body missing `what`, with verifyDocument's reason;\n   - the page text holds the CSP exactly, no `src=`, no `href=` to anywhere, no `fetch(`, and no `http://` or `https://` outside the spec's own words;\n   - a body whose `what` holds `</script>` cannot close the block: parse the page's inline script with `new vm.Script` and read the JSON block back equal to the body.\ntest/receipt-page.test.mjs, using a receipt from vectors/receipts:\n   - receiptPage gives a page that embeds the document unchanged, parses as above, and holds the CSP;\n   - a document with one changed character is refused by the command;\n   - a receipt where one key signed every role yields the sentence from docs/design.md, and one with different keys does not.\nA browser cannot run in your check, so keep every decision in functions the tests can call, and keep the page's own script to wiring.\n\nWHAT MUST PASS. Tick's check on your commit, including every existing test unchanged. Commit, call tick_check, and report with tick_report. Add no dependency. If a test can only pass by changing a file not in your list, ask for it with tick_widen rather than weakening anything."},"order_id":"01a190eb-3cdc-741e-98bb-cde27a8405ed","schema":"tick.work-order.v1","signature":"mj60VnWtWGGGSRnxX+Hu0tEPxmtGs9P/8hd+SBR2CHjnaDAkGL3ImPyn9R0Y9CqISN/I+kOQOjbULKenFXn7Cg=="}},"receipt_id":"01a190eb-3cdc-741e-98bb-cde27a8405ed","schema":"tick.receipt.v2","signature":"F8xoBGalFcmsY4gIhwvnr9QvN555MdlYgX6kW7UoX+MQ/wlZJC/IwRQMg0gYs8rJOIuWksPa4coMUZ/sV+70Cw=="}]}
